export const PRIVACY_POLICY_MD = "# Privacy Policy\n\n**DaLesson Tutoring Management Platform**\n\n**Last Updated: October 30, 2026**\n\n**Effective Date: January 31, 2026**\n\n---\n\n## Introduction\n\nDaLesson (\"we,\" \"our,\" or \"us\") is committed to protecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your information when you use our tutoring management platform, available on iOS, Android, and web applications (collectively, the \"Service\").\n\nPlease read this Privacy Policy carefully. By accessing or using the Service, you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agree to be bound by this Privacy Policy. If you do not agree with the terms of this Privacy Policy, please do not access the Service.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Information We Collect\n\nWe collect information that you provide directly to us, information collected automatically when you use the Service, and information from third-party sources.\n\n### 1.1 Personal Information You Provide\n\nWhen you register for an account or use our Service, we may collect the following categories of personal information:\n\n**Account Information:**\n- Email address\n- Phone number\n- Password (encrypted)\n- Account type (tutor or parent)\n\n**Profile Information:**\n- Full name\n- Profile photograph (optional)\n- Contact preferences\n\n**Student Information:**\n- Student names\n- Ages and birthdates\n- Grade levels\n- School information\n- Subject areas of instruction\n- Learning notes and progress information\n- Special accommodations or learning needs\n\n**Scheduling Information:**\n- Lesson schedules and appointments\n- Availability preferences\n- Session history\n- Reschedule and cancellation records\n\n**Communication Data:**\n- Messages between tutors and parents\n- Lesson notes and feedback\n- Notification preferences\n\n**Payment Information:**\n- Billing address\n- Payment history and invoice records\n- Subscription status\n\n*Note: Credit card numbers, bank account details, and other sensitive financial information are collected and processed directly by our payment processor, Stripe, and are not stored on our servers.*\n\n### 1.2 Information Collected Automatically\n\nWhen you access or use the Service, we automatically collect certain information, including:\n\n**Device Information:**\n- Device type and model\n- Operating system and version\n- Unique device identifiers\n- Mobile network information\n\n**Usage Information:**\n- Features accessed and actions taken\n- Time and date of access\n- Session duration\n- Referring URLs and exit pages\n\n**Log Data:**\n- IP address\n- Browser type and version\n- Access times and dates\n- Error logs and crash reports\n\n### 1.3 Information from Third-Party Sources\n\nWe may receive information about you from third-party sources, including:\n\n- **Authentication providers:** If you sign in using a third-party service (e.g., Google, Apple), we receive your name and email address from that service\n- **Payment processor:** Transaction confirmations and payment status from Stripe\n\n---\n\n## 2. How We Use Your Information\n\nWe use the information we collect for the following purposes:\n\n### 2.1 Providing and Improving the Service\n\n- Create and manage your account\n- Facilitate scheduling and lesson management\n- Enable communication between tutors and parents\n- Process payments and generate invoices\n- Send transactional notifications (lesson reminders, schedule changes, payment confirmations)\n- Provide customer support\n- Analyze usage patterns to improve the Service\n- Develop new features and functionality\n\n### 2.2 Communication\n\n- Send service-related announcements and updates\n- Respond to your inquiries and requests\n- Send promotional communications (with your consent, where required)\n- Notify you of changes to our policies or terms\n\n### 2.3 Safety and Security\n\n- Detect, prevent, and address fraud, abuse, or security issues\n- Enforce our Terms of Service\n- Protect the rights, property, and safety of our users and the public\n- Comply with legal obligations\n\n### 2.4 Legal Compliance\n\n- Fulfill legal and regulatory requirements\n- Respond to lawful requests from public authorities\n- Establish, exercise, or defend legal claims\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Storage and Security\n\n### 3.1 Infrastructure and Storage\n\nYour data is stored using industry-leading cloud infrastructure:\n\n- **Database:** PostgreSQL database hosted on Supabase, which runs on Amazon Web Services (AWS) infrastructure\n- **Authentication:** Secure authentication services provided by Supabase Auth\n- **File Storage:** Secure cloud storage through Supabase Storage (AWS S3)\n- **Data Centers:** Your data is stored in secure data centers located in the United States\n\n### 3.2 Security Measures\n\nWe implement comprehensive security measures to protect your information:\n\n**Technical Safeguards:**\n- Encryption of data in transit using TLS 1.2 or higher\n- Encryption of data at rest using AES-256 encryption\n- Secure token-based authentication\n- Row-Level Security (RLS) policies ensuring users can only access authorized data\n- Regular security updates and patches\n\n**Operational Safeguards:**\n- Access controls limiting data access to authorized personnel\n- Regular security audits and assessments\n- Incident response procedures\n- Employee security training\n\n**Application Security:**\n- Secure credential storage using platform-specific secure storage (iOS Keychain, Android Keystore)\n- Session management and automatic timeout\n- Input validation and sanitization\n\n### 3.3 Data Breach Notification\n\nIn the event of a data breach that affects your personal information, we will notify you and any applicable regulatory authorities as required by law, within 72 hours of becoming aware of the breach.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Third-Party Services\n\nWe use the following third-party services to operate the Service. Each of these services has their own privacy policies governing the use of your information:\n\n### 4.1 Supabase\n\nWe use Supabase for database hosting, authentication, and file storage. Supabase processes data on our behalf as a data processor.\n\n- Privacy Policy: https://supabase.com/privacy\n\n### 4.2 Stripe\n\nWe use Stripe for payment processing. When you make a payment, your payment information is collected and processed directly by Stripe.\n\n- Privacy Policy: https://stripe.com/privacy\n\n### 4.3 Apple (iOS App Distribution)\n\nIf you download our iOS app, Apple may collect certain information as described in their privacy policy.\n\n- Privacy Policy: https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/\n\n### 4.4 Google (Android App Distribution)\n\nIf you download our Android app, Google may collect certain information as described in their privacy policy.\n\n- Privacy Policy: https://policies.google.com/privacy\n\n### 4.5 Resend (Email Delivery)\n\nWe use Resend to send transactional emails, such as parent invitations, lesson reschedule notices, and payment reminders. Resend receives the recipient's email address and the content of the email.\n\n- Privacy Policy: https://resend.com/legal/privacy-policy\n\n### 4.6 Expo and Apple/Google Push Services (Push Notifications)\n\nIf you allow notifications, we use Expo's push notification service, which relays notifications through Apple Push Notification service and Firebase Cloud Messaging. These services receive a device push token and the notification content.\n\n- Privacy Policy: https://expo.dev/privacy\n\n### 4.7 Telegram (Optional Weekly Recap)\n\nIf a tutor chooses to link a Telegram account, we send that tutor a weekly summary of their lessons and payments through Telegram. Nothing is sent to Telegram unless the tutor turns this feature on, and it can be turned off at any time.\n\n- Privacy Policy: https://telegram.org/privacy\n\n### 4.8 Analytics and Advertising\n\nWe do not currently use third-party analytics, advertising, or tracking SDKs in our apps, and we do not track you across other companies' apps or websites. If we add analytics in the future, we will update this policy first.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Data Retention\n\nWe retain your personal information for as long as necessary to fulfill the purposes outlined in this Privacy Policy, unless a longer retention period is required or permitted by law.\n\n### 5.1 Retention Periods\n\n| Data Type | Retention Period |\n|-----------|-----------------|\n| Account information | Duration of account + 30 days after deletion request |\n| Student information | Duration of account + 30 days after deletion request |\n| Lesson history | 7 years (for tax and legal purposes) |\n| Payment records | 7 years (for tax and legal purposes) |\n| Messages | 3 years or until account deletion |\n| Usage logs | 90 days |\n| Security logs | 1 year |\n\n### 5.2 Account Deletion\n\nYou can delete your account at any time from inside the app (**More → Profile → Delete Account**) or by emailing privacy@dalesson.app.\n\nWhen you request account deletion:\n- Your account will be deactivated immediately\n- Personal data will be deleted within 30 days\n- Certain data may be retained as required by law (e.g., payment records for tax purposes)\n- Anonymized, aggregated data may be retained indefinitely for analytics purposes\n\n---\n\n## 6. Your Rights\n\nYou have certain rights regarding your personal information, subject to applicable law.\n\n### 6.1 Access\n\nYou have the right to request access to the personal information we hold about you. You can access most of your data directly through your account settings.\n\n### 6.2 Correction\n\nYou have the right to request that we correct inaccurate or incomplete personal information. You can update most information directly in your account settings.\n\n### 6.3 Deletion\n\nYou have the right to request deletion of your personal information, subject to certain exceptions (e.g., legal retention requirements).\n\n### 6.4 Data Portability\n\nYou have the right to receive a copy of your personal information in a structured, commonly used, and machine-readable format (such as JSON or CSV).\n\n### 6.5 Restriction of Processing\n\nYou have the right to request that we restrict processing of your personal information under certain circumstances.\n\n### 6.6 Objection\n\nYou have the right to object to processing of your personal information for direct marketing purposes.\n\n### 6.7 Withdrawal of Consent\n\nWhere we process your personal information based on consent, you have the right to withdraw that consent at any time.\n\n### 6.8 Exercising Your Rights\n\nTo exercise any of these rights, please contact us at:\n- Email: privacy@dalesson.app\n\nWe will respond to your request within 30 days. We may request additional information to verify your identity before processing your request.\n\n---\n\n## 7. California Privacy Rights (CCPA)\n\nIf you are a California resident, you have additional rights under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) and the California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA).\n\n### 7.1 Right to Know\n\nYou have the right to request that we disclose:\n- The categories of personal information we have collected about you\n- The categories of sources from which we collected your personal information\n- The business or commercial purpose for collecting your personal information\n- The categories of third parties with whom we share your personal information\n- The specific pieces of personal information we have collected about you\n\n### 7.2 Right to Delete\n\nYou have the right to request deletion of personal information we have collected from you, subject to certain exceptions.\n\n### 7.3 Right to Correct\n\nYou have the right to request correction of inaccurate personal information.\n\n### 7.4 Right to Opt-Out of Sale/Sharing\n\n**We do not sell your personal information.** We do not share your personal information for cross-context behavioral advertising.\n\n### 7.5 Right to Non-Discrimination\n\nWe will not discriminate against you for exercising any of your CCPA rights.\n\n### 7.6 Authorized Agents\n\nYou may designate an authorized agent to submit requests on your behalf. We may require verification that you authorized the agent to act on your behalf.\n\n### 7.7 Categories of Personal Information\n\nIn the preceding 12 months, we have collected the following categories of personal information as defined by the CCPA:\n\n| Category | Examples | Collected |\n|----------|----------|-----------|\n| Identifiers | Name, email, phone, IP address | Yes |\n| Personal Information (Cal. Civ. Code 1798.80) | Name, address, phone, education | Yes |\n| Protected Classifications | Age (for students) | Yes |\n| Commercial Information | Payment records, subscription history | Yes |\n| Internet/Network Activity | Usage data, browsing history | Yes |\n| Geolocation Data | General location from IP address | Yes |\n| Professional Information | Tutor credentials | Yes |\n| Education Information | Student grades, progress | Yes |\n| Inferences | Learning preferences | Yes |\n\n### 7.8 Contact for California Residents\n\nCalifornia residents may contact us at:\n- Email: privacy@dalesson.app\n- Include \"California Privacy Request\" in the subject line\n\n---\n\n## 8. Children's Privacy (COPPA Compliance)\n\n### 8.1 Children's Information\n\nDaLesson is a tutoring management platform designed for tutors to manage their tutoring business. While the Service stores information about students, including children under the age of 13, this information is provided by tutors and parents, not directly by children.\n\n### 8.2 Parental Consent\n\n**Tutors' Responsibility:** Tutors using the Service are responsible for obtaining appropriate consent from parents or legal guardians before entering any student information into the system. By entering student information, tutors represent and warrant that they have obtained the necessary parental consent.\n\n**Parents' Consent:** When parents create accounts, they consent to the collection and use of their children's information as described in this Privacy Policy.\n\n### 8.3 What We Do Not Collect from Children\n\n- We do not allow children under 13 to create accounts\n- We do not collect personal information directly from children\n- We do not target advertising to children\n\n### 8.4 Parental Rights\n\nParents have the right to:\n- Review their child's information stored in the Service\n- Request deletion of their child's information\n- Refuse further collection of their child's information\n\nTo exercise these rights, parents should contact their tutor directly or email us at privacy@dalesson.app.\n\n### 8.5 Student Data Protection\n\nWe are committed to protecting student data and comply with applicable student data privacy laws, including:\n- The Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA), where applicable\n- State student data privacy laws\n\n---\n\n## 9. Changes to This Privacy Policy\n\nWe may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our practices, technology, legal requirements, or other factors.\n\n### 9.1 Notification of Changes\n\n- **Material Changes:** We will notify you of material changes by email and/or by posting a prominent notice in the Service at least 30 days before the changes take effect\n- **Minor Changes:** Non-material changes will be posted on this page with an updated \"Last Updated\" date\n\n### 9.2 Continued Use\n\nYour continued use of the Service after the effective date of any changes constitutes your acceptance of the revised Privacy Policy.\n\n### 9.3 Review\n\nWe encourage you to review this Privacy Policy periodically to stay informed about how we are protecting your information.\n\n---\n\n## 10. International Data Transfers\n\n### 10.1 Data Location\n\nYour personal information is stored and processed in the United States. If you are accessing the Service from outside the United States, please be aware that your information may be transferred to, stored, and processed in the United States.\n\n### 10.2 Legal Basis for Transfer\n\nBy using the Service, you consent to the transfer of your information to the United States. We take appropriate measures to ensure that your personal information receives an adequate level of protection.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Do Not Track Signals\n\nSome web browsers have a \"Do Not Track\" feature that signals to websites that you do not want to have your online activities tracked. The Service does not currently respond to \"Do Not Track\" signals.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Contact Information\n\nIf you have questions, concerns, or requests regarding this Privacy Policy or our data practices, please contact us:\n\n**Email:** privacy@dalesson.app\n\n**Response Time:** We will respond to your inquiry within 30 days.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Governing Law\n\nThis Privacy Policy is governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of Delaware, United States, without regard to its conflict of law provisions.\n\n---\n\n*This Privacy Policy was last updated on October 30, 2026.*";

